emergency department with sudden-onset
severe epigastric pain. On examination, she
has a blood pressure of 90/55mmHg, a heart
rate of 110 bpm, and a respiratory rate of 22
breaths per minute. There is abdominal
guarding and rigidity, as well as marked
tenderness and rebound tenderness over the
epigastric area. A chest X-ray reveals free air
under the right hemi-diaphragm. Based on
clinical findings, a perforated peptic ulcer is
diagnosed and the patient is planned for
emergency laparotomy. She is on warfarin
due to deep vein thrombosis (DVT) that
developed two weeks ago. Which one of the
following is the most appropriate next step in
