clinic with pallor and dark urine after he took
cotrimoxazole for an acute respiratory
infection. Blood investigations are significant
for hemoglobin of 90 g/L and a reticulocyte
count of 5%. Both direct and indirect Coombs
tests are negative. Serum electrophoresis
shows type A hemoglobin. There is no family
history of such a presentation. Which one of
