Emergency Department with generalized severe
pain in his limbs and joints. He is a known case
of sickle cell disease and has just arrived from
Paris to Melbourne after a long flight. On a
scale of 1 to 10, Peter rates the pain as 7. He
denies any breathlessness or chest pain. On
examination, he has a blood pressure of 140/87
mmHg, a pulse rate of 104 bpm, a respiratory
rate of 18 breaths per minute, and a
temperature of 36.9°C. The only remarkable
exam finding is the generalized tenderness on
palpation of his muscles, bones, and joints of
upper and lower limbs. Which one of the
following would be the next best step in
