clinical grounds, TB is a likely diagnosis.

(Option D) High resolution CT scan of the chest
has no role in diagnosis of TB and is not
indicated unless the diagnosis is not certain or
other diagnoses than TB are considered...

(Option E) Starting the patient on full-dose 4-
drug therapy for tuberculosis is indicated in this
patient due to high possibility of TB as the
diagnosis, but it should be delayed until samples
are taken because antibiotics, if used prior to
testing, may alter test results, mostly in form of
false negativity.

