with complaints of fever, joint pain and a
generalized rash all over his body. His fever and
other symptoms started this morning, five days
after he returned from Thailand. On
examination, maculopapular rash over his limbs
and trunk are noted. Despite generalized severe
joint pain, no arthritis is noted on exam.
Abdominal exam is normal and there is no
lymphadenopathy. A full blood exam (FBE) is
performed, the result of which is as follows:
e Hb: 135 g/L (normal: 130-180 g/L)
© RBC: 5x10°/mm?® (4.5x10°-6.5x10%
mm )
© MCV: 85 fL (76-96 fL)
© WCC: 3100/mm? (4000-11000/ mm
© Platelet: 75000/mm?* (150,000-
400,000/mm?)
3)
