Darwin (Northern Territory) with complaints of
rash and malaise and fatigue for the past few
weeks. He is originally from Asia but has been
living in Darwin for the past 3 months as a
backpacker. On examination, vital signs
including temperature are within normal limits.
He has a maculopapular rash over the soles
and palms that are non-pruritic, and cervical,
axillary, and inguinal lymphadenopathy which is
not tender. There are also two small alopecic
patches on his head. Which one of the following
is the most appropriate treatment option for
him?','{"A":"Doxycycline.","B":"Benzyl penicillin.","C":"Azithromycin.","D":"Procaine penicillin.","E":"Intramuscular ceftriaxone."}','B',NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 INFECTIOUS DISEASE (2).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-5afbbbbc3725","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"8c9272c65c35fdc76c97","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 INFECTIOUS DISEASE (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 INFECTIOUS DISEASE (2).pdf","source_page":114,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"48127b14d991310d6799","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":691,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"8c9272c65c35fdc76c97","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 INFECTIOUS DISEASE (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 INFECTIOUS DISEASE (2).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":114,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Infectious Disease","stem":"A 22-year-old man presents to your practice in\nDarwin (Northern Territory) with complaints of\nrash and malaise and fatigue for the past few\nweeks. He is originally from Asia but has been\nliving in Darwin for the past 3 months as a\nbackpacker. On examination, vital signs\nincluding temperature are within normal limits.\nHe has a maculopapular rash over the soles\nand palms that are non-pruritic, and cervical,\naxillary, and inguinal lymphadenopathy which is\nnot tender. There are also two small alopecic\npatches on his head. Which one of the following\nis the most appropriate treatment option for\nhim?","options":{"A":"Doxycycline.","B":"Benzyl penicillin.","C":"Azithromycin.","D":"Procaine penic